  "name": "Noodle Biomedical Literature Discovery MCP",
  "alternateName": [
    "noodle-mcp"
  ],
  "description": "MCP server for source-linked biomedical literature discovery across a PubMed-derived corpus, from Helena Bioinformatics. Lets LLM agents search by natural language or identifiers, retrieve publication records, check corpus coverage, and explore bounded citation and semantic-graph neighbourhoods with provenance (seven tools over a read-only Streamable HTTP endpoint). The Apache-2.0 repository holds the official adapter, packaging, a 60-prompt benchmark, CI, a Dockerfile, and a citable DOI. Important: the service itself runs at a hosted endpoint (api.helena.bio/noodle) rather than from the open repository — the adapter is open, the backing service is vendor-operated. Accepts no patient, private case, credential, or uploaded content.",
  "url": "https://noodle.helena.bio",
